A window holding NaN or infinite values is an error for a foundation model, when extracting embeddings, fitting and predicting, and the error names the windows. Such a window gave a NaN embedding, and with `normalize_embeddings=True`, the default, the L2 normalisation turned it into a vector of zeros: it was kept as an ordinary embedding and pulled the recording embedding toward zero, with no error and no warning. The normalisation now maps only a zero vector to zeros, so a NaN embedding a model produces stays NaN.
